WEBVTT

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.090
Uh. Um...

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:47.950
Soichiro, I'll be alone
untill spring.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:49.840
Huh?!

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.860
The manager
really said that?

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.560
Very clearly.
Right in front of me.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.500
But she didn't mention
your name, did she?

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.150
She could have been
talking about Coach Mitaka.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.180
No, she...

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.080
Thank you for your patronage.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.970
Our next stop will be Kanda.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.220
We're gettin' off, Godai.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:30.910
Yeah.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.900
This is Kanda.
Kanda Station.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:34.780
Please make way for
those getting off.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.750
Please stay clear
of the door.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.220
We're getting off!
Please!

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:41.830
Excuse us!

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:42.740
Please!

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:46.300
Made it!

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.960
Yagami, what's the matter?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.650
You didn't even
eat your lunch.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.560
You're not yourself.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.990
Did something happen
between you and that widow?

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.190
Not really.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.590
Then what? Something
about Mr. Godai?

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.990
That's it, isn't it?!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.770
Tell us!

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.400
Mr. Godai seemed
really optimistic

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.710
going on his
job hunt today.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.270
He hasn't gotten
a job yet?!

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.340
That's why Yagami's.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.310
Daddy hasn't budged.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.550
Who knows how
he feels about me.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.460
So the fact that you've left
home hasn't helped at all

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:40.990
So what?

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.150
At least now you're living
under the same roof

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.330
as your beloved Mr. Godai.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.800
You're so lucky!

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:47.960
Stop it.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.090
I left home because I really
care about Mr. Godai.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.430
But if you dilly-dally, he
might find a job on his own.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.000
You don't want that.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.240
Right

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.130
Right. You don't want that.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:01.620
I know.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.840
But I want him
to get a job.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.380
Do you really?

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.780
But it's true that a part of me
doesn't want him to get a Job.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:18.020
As a woman, it's sad not to
be able to help the man I love.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:22.430
And I also want to make up
for what happened before.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.020
Yeah. The company you
hooked him up with went bankrupt.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.500
I know the pain
you must feel.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.610
Large draft beer!

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.550
So you decided to go with
the trading company.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:42.310
I had three offers. It was
hard to turn down the other two.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.880
I figured I'd be able
to live overseas

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.480
If I joined a trading firm.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.680
I see.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.180
So now we all have
a job lined up.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.430
Let's toast to that!

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.250
Cheers!

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.370
It's great.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:03.370
Ha! Trading firm?
Overseas? Who cares.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.000
Even second- or third-rate
companies won't consider us.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:11.350
Can't help it. We'll
Just have to keep looking.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.200
You can say that because
you've got a backup plan.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:17.790
Backup plan?

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.380
Yagami, your super-connection.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:23.420
Stop it. That's
not even an option.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.950
Sure it is.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.190
After all, you've got
his daughter as a hostage.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:33.040
Shut up. People might
think you're serious.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.470
She decided to come
on her own.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.850
If I were actually
counting on her,

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.760
I wouldn't bother making
the rounds with you.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:41.570
Is that the truth?

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:42.770
It's the truth.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.240
Really?

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.910
Yes, it is.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.880
IT'S THE TRUTH!!!

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:05.300
Then how come you're still leisurely
doing part-time at the preschool?

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.190
You don't have time for that.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:12.600
"Leisurely"? I'm working
In between my job-hunt.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.390
I like spending time
with kids.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:20.940
While I'm with them, I can
forget about finding a job.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.850
It's a form of escape,
Isn't it?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:23.950
Escape?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.660
Master! Another large draft!

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:27.660
Sure

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:32.790
Let's drink and forget about it!
Whaddaya say?! C'mon, Godai!

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.740
I'm back, Soichiro.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.220
I'm...

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:56.270
Oh? These shoes...?

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.290
Oh , it's you, Manager.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.080
Welcome back.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:06.120
What're you doing?
That's Godai's.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.360
It's okay. Please.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:11.690
Yotsuya?!

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:13.860
Good evening.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.260
We're here.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:17.870
Hello.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.690
How 'bout a cold one
after your bath?

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.410
No thank you.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:27.640
Manager, have you heard
anything from Mr. Godai?

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:28.510
No.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:29.370
Oh .

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.290
Didn't I tell you?
He had no luck today, either.

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:35.880
Isn't that great, Yagami?

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.500
At least, it's back
to square one.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.870
Is it somehow good for you
if Godai doesn't get a job?

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.410
It's an inside story.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:47.450
Right?

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.060
I'm quite sure
he and Sakamoto

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:53.240
are drinking their sorrow
away as we speak.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.060
Can't you do something
for him already?

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:59.870
Yeah. Isn't that why you left home?

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:02.880
I know.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:10.360
Yagami, maybe you shouldn't
cause your father so much grief.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.690
Manager, do you
have a problem

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:17.100
with Mr. Godai getting a job
with my father's influence?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.270
N-No, I just--

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.740
You just what?!

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.830
I Just think that's
for Godai to decide.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:25.430
That's right.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:30.060
Yagami, your father can
easily help a person or two.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.300
Yeah. He's the
Personnel Director

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.720
of a huge corporation.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.950
Wow, your dad's
Impressive, Yagami!

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:39.220
You know why we're
here, don't you?

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:40.250
Huh?

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:44.280
Maybe you're not
pressuring him enough.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:48.330
I think you need to do
something more drastic.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:51.460
Why don't you move
into Mr. Godai's apartment?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.120
Huh?!

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.150
Force him to marry you!

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:01.300
S-Stop it! This isn't
a joke, you know.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:04.780
You've got to build up a case.
There's no other way.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.820
Are you serious?

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:23.790
Godai never came home
Iast night, huh?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:28.760
Maybe he have no choice
but to rely on Yagami's father.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:43.250
Or he'll have to wait another
year for the next chance?

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.250
Manager, are you going
to make that tree bald?

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:50.320
Oops! It's rather
clean-cut, isn't it?

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:53.830
It's about time my washer
is done. I better go.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.730
It can't be easy being caught

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.420
between a high school girl
and a job hunt.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:32.440
Godai? Yes, he's here.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.080
No, he seems like
his usual self.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.040
Would you like
to speak to him?

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.500
That won't be necessary.
Thank you.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.750
Thanks for making
those blocks.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:55.960
That's what the kids
love to play with most.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.490
Hello, Principal!

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:01.240
Hello, boys and girls.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:03.830
Do you like those blocks?

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.280
Great I'm so glad.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.170
Go back to playing, children.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:10.530
Yes!

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.760
Godai , won't you bring
that creativity

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:19.380
into the upcoming fun fest
by joining the committee?

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.170
Me?

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:26.640
We always have the same old
game equipment and decorations.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:27.820
How about it?

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.540
Can you come up with
ideas the kids would love?

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.150
But.

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:37.150
Of course, I want your primary
focus to be your job search,

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:38.500
but won't you help us?

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:40.000
Sure.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.870
Are you going to be at
the Fun Fest, Mr. Godai?

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:44.340
Are you?!

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.110
Of course, he will

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.370
If there's anything special
you want to do at the Fun Fest,

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.840
you Just ask
Mr. Godai, all right?

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.190
I want to sing and dance!

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:53.370
I want the Ball Toss Game!

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.000
I want the Donut-eating Game!

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:58.590
Hold it! One person
at a time, please.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.270
I can't listen to
everybody at once.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.190
All on target!

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:34.010
Right.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.650
It's good to have you back.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.710
It's my home, after all

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:57.480
That's right. There's no
place like home, is there?

00:12:58.130 --> 00:12:59.810
I love Mom's cooking.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.290
It's so much more fun when
you're here, Ibuki

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:11.170
When it's just the two of us,
it's like a wake.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.070
Right, dear?

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.750
Who knew Ibuki can
cook for herself.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:19.330
I'm pretty good, you know.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.850
Why don't you cook for
your dad sometime?

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.410
Sure. Thank you for dinner.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.040
Would you like
some pear, Ibuki?

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.160
No. I better
be heading back.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:31.880
Heading back?!

00:13:32.460 --> 00:13:33.550
Of course.

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:36.420
I haven't gotten a letter of
referral for Mr. Godai yet

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.450
Then why did you come home?

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:45.910
I wanted to eat
with you both. Bye!

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:52.380
After I'm done with Maison Ikkoku,
I'll never trouble you again.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.810
Wait, Ibuki!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:58.040
What do you think
you're doing?

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.670
I'm counting on you, Mom.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.180
Bye!

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.480
Hold it, Ibuki!

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.370
Dear, she's gone.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:11.760
I know!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.770
It was so nice to
eat as a family.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:29.210
Welcome home.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.150
Hi.

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:32.170
You're home quite late.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.160
They've asked me to be
a committee member

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:35.440
of the preschool Fun Fest.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:36.680
There's a lot of
preparation involved.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.760
Committee member?

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:44.270
You have time for that,
Mr. Job-hunter?

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:47.600
You're counting on that girl's father's
letter of recommendation, aren't you?

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:51.420
No way! I'm not.

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:53.530
Where is Yagami?

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.230
She's not back yet.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:56.910
It's almost 10pm!

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:59.480
We can't call her home.

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:01.440
I'll go look for her
near the station.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:03.210
You're worried about her?

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:04.650
Of course I am!

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:07.540
She's in high school. She
shouldn't be out this late!

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:10.310
You didn't seem
to care before.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:13.530
His future job rests on
her now, that's why.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:15.860
I'm not counting on her!

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.100
You don't have to lie to us.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.680
Anyway, I'm going out
to look for her.

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:22.900
Sorry I'm so late!

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:27.660
Yagami! Where have you been?
It's late.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.700
You were worried about me?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.850
I went home for a while.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:35.670
Did you bring back a letter
of recommendation?

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:36.880
No.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.380
But It's just
a matter of time now.

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.650
Way to go.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:44.490
Isn't that great, Godai?

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:46.420
You better be grateful

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:49.160
I told you, I'm not
counting on any help!

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.240
How about an
early celebration?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.560
Let's! Let's!

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:56.450
I'd be happy to celebrate
Godai's employment any time!

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:59.740
Hey! I'm not employed yet.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:04.570
Loosen up. You ARE getting
a job in the end.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.610
Never turn down a favor.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:23.890
There!

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:40.440
May we move the Fun Fest
meeting to 3pm?

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:44.210
I have to attend a job search
seminar at my college.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.110
Sure.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.040
You seem so busy.

00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:51.780
You should have declined to
be on the committee.

00:16:52.290 --> 00:16:54.580
But I love things like that

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:58.260
Do you really want to
become an office worker?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:04.960
I'm not sure...but I don't
know what else I'd do.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:06.930
Why don't you become
a preschool teacher?

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:07.760
Me?

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.230
I think you're perfect
for this job.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:11.910
You've got a strong
sense of responsibility,

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:14.440
and you're a natural at
reaching out to children.

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:15.610
You think so?

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:17.590
I sure do.

00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:18.880
Why don't you think about

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.620
taking the certification
exam next summer?

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:21.510
But.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:25.450
Don't try to sway a man in
the midst of his job search.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.020
Oh, but.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:32.290
Don't you think it would be so much better
than an office Job, Godai?

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.830
I-I

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:36.100
I better get going...

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:38.420
Sakamoto, come
Join us for a drink.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:39.790
Sure!

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.660
Finish your job first, man.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:42.390
Shucks.

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:44.230
C'mon. Just one beer.

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:45.070
NO.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:47.500
The fun fest is tomorrow.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.570
You're such a pushover.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.370
They may call you
a committee member,

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:53.700
but they're using you
as a laborer.

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.790
The kids' parents will surely
reward you with liquor?

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:58.710
No.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.480
If I can make the kids happy,
that's reward enough for me.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:10.260
Daddy?!

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:12.570
Hello, everyone.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:17.960
Godai, here's a letter
of recommendation.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.810
Thank you, Daddy!

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:28.070
What's the matter? Can't you
at least smile or something?

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.980
He's so happy
he's speechless.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.850
Godai , congratulations
on your employment!

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.420
Banzai!

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:38.860
No!

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:41.180
Congrats, Godai.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:42.710
Bravo!

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:44.690
Good things come
to those who bait

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:51.300
How about thanking
Director Yagami, Godai?

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:52.500
But.

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:55.020
What are you waiting for?

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:56.930
You don't need to thank me.

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:58.870
But I'm taking Ibuki
home with me.

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:00.600
Let's go.

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:02.790
No! I'm not going home yet.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:03.500
What?!

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:07.710
I told you when I left home
that I'm not coming back

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.020
until Mr. Godai is
employed for sure.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.210
I selected this company.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.090
There's no chance this firm
wll go under. I guarantee it.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:20.260
No. Mr. Godai's future
is riding on this.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.480
You're coming home!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.430
You're starting to
make me very angry!

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:26.340
What are you doing?

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:27.110
Ibuki!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.300
Stop it!

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.910
I can't accept this.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:38.010
What about Ibuki?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:41.270
Yagami, you go home
with your father.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.210
Why won't you
take it, Mr. Godai?

00:20:44.690 --> 00:20:48.860
The truth is, I want this
letter of recommendation

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.690
more than anything.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.800
But I can't accept it.

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:56.370
I'm afraid this may
take me somewhere

00:20:56.440 --> 00:20:59.140
I don't want to be.

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:03.580
I want to choose my
own path to my future.

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:05.880
It's my life, after all

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.980
Mr. Godai?

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:10.950
Understood.

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:17.320
Godai , you're REALLY
giving this back?

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:18.380
You won't regret it?!

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:20.210
No.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.950
Sir! May I please have this?

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:25.600
My name is Sakamoto.
I'm Godai's friend.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.230
Like Godai, I've been
desperately looking for a Job.

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:31.160
Please help a man in need
and allow me to have this!

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:32.930
Please! I beg of you!

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:35.500
But.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:45.150
What's wrong with Godai?
He could have secured a job.

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:47.210
He put on a good show.

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.250
It's going to be
quiet around here

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:52.180
without our playmate Yagami.

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:54.360
Let's drink some more.

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:55.560
Let's.

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:56.540
Let's!

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.540
I wonder if I did
the right thing?

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:14.340
I think a part of me is
regretting what I've done.

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:19.180
But work is something
you do for life.

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:21.220
You're right.

00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:25.020
There's nothing worse
than being stuck in a job you hate.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:25.820
Right.

00:22:29.410 --> 00:22:32.730
Won't you come to
tomorrow's Fun Fest?

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:33.910
Sure.

00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:52.390
C'mon! C'mon!

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:54.770
You can do it!

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:07.160
Keep going!
Just a little more!

00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:51.340
Girly cabaret?!

00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:53.530
We can drink every night!

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:55.380
No need to hold back!

00:23:55.480 --> 00:23:57.970
Huh!? You can't be serious!

00:23:58.120 --> 00:23:59.340
Sure...

00:23:59.420 --> 00:24:03.080
Next: "I'm Not Sayin'!
The Cabaret Chronicles"

00:24:03.180 --> 00:24:05.090
You don't want us.

00:24:05.160 --> 00:24:06.880
to tell the manager, do you?
